{"id": "EUVD-2026-103552", "enisaUuid": "7f054705-6072-35fc-812b-0c8582b91795", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: arm64: Validate the SVE vector length in pkvm_vcpu_init_sve()\n\npkvm_vcpu_init_sve() clamps only the upper bound of the host-provided\nsve_max_vl, so an invalid vector length reaches sve_state_size_from_vl()\nand the WARN_ON() there, which is fatal at EL2. The existing\n!sve_state_size test rejects such a length, but only after the macro has\nrun.\n\nCheck sve_vl_valid() before deriving the state size. A valid length\ncannot yield a zero size, so the !sve_state_size test goes with it.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:20:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:08", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/faf66e55e87498ab4bf88cdf9a629e61b3f2d3bc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bae3e4493046de4fefa15f809d9b8dc114e84a3d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a2eb10795a1e495aebc7f829ccecb72c05b4fd9"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jqwq-p3w6-jffx", "CVE-2026-98638"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "17546406-e77b-3663-9764-58a15df3bd73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "25465391-d8ba-334a-8493-aac496411033", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5db1bef933427aa467ad89c7b695a84a6b4afe16 <faf66e55e87498ab4bf88cdf9a629e61b3f2d3bc"}, {"id": "31a5f75e-0bc2-389c-854c-f36b638a3954", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5db1bef933427aa467ad89c7b695a84a6b4afe16 <2a2eb10795a1e495aebc7f829ccecb72c05b4fd9"}, {"id": "36430ac4-1699-3a75-a427-57d49ae71e0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "77a7b364-3b67-39f3-a842-6f43aef55800", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5db1bef933427aa467ad89c7b695a84a6b4afe16 <bae3e4493046de4